,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | |  | | $y$ | $-2$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P(X=0,Y=-2)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)$\n- $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n- $X$ and $Y$ are independent" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388876 1113 #uuid "54cab6ac-9169-51f6-a0e0-b782401a693c" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388876 1145 "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=-2)=f(0,-2)=\\frac{1}{4}.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=-2)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,2) & =\\frac{5}{12}=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,-2) & =\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2) & ✓ \\\\ f(3,2) & =\\frac{5}{24}=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388878 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388879 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388880 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388881 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388882 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1041 "selection" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388878 13194139536203 true] [17592186388877 1110 #uuid "37369e50-ee96-592c-8beb-e18c62d08f1a" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388878 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536203 true] [17592186388878 1111 #uuid "1df92081-cbd8-550f-a2a5-44e2bf8d816d" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388879 1034 "I only" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536203 true] [17592186388879 1111 #uuid "ffb74ec0-5ae1-528c-a2df-83520cfee88e" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388880 1034 "III only" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536203 true] [17592186388880 1111 #uuid "fd574fbd-ef47-5705-acce-70b1c840546f" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388881 1034 "I and II only" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536203 true] [17592186388881 1111 #uuid "ca9b0e1c-e4e6-560e-be2c-bf446024134a" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388882 1034 "None of the statements" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536203 true] [17592186388882 1111 #uuid "8a03441b-8699-50ae-a513-730107fa88a2" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388883 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388884 13194139536203 true] [17592186388883 1089 "q-163617" 13194139536203 true] [17592186388883 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536203 true] [17592186388883 1100 "| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ 